// =============================================================================
// அகநானூறு · Akanāṉūṟu — The Four Hundred Interior (Love) Poems
// =============================================================================
// An anthology of 400 Sangam-era poems on the inner life of love (akam).
// Each poem belongs to one of five landscapes (tiṇai):
//   குறிஞ்சி (Kuṟiñci) — mountains — the secret tryst before marriage
//   முல்லை  (Mullai)   — forest    — patient waiting
//   மருதம்  (Marutam)  — fields    — lovers' quarrels & infidelity
//   நெய்தல் (Neytal)   — seashore  — anxious longing & separation by sea
//   பாலை   (Pālai)    — wasteland — separation by desert journey
//
// The anthology is also organized as three sub-collections (interleaved):
//   களிற்றியானை நிரை (poems 1, 6, 11... — pālai)
//   மணிமிடை பவளம்   (poems 2, 4, 6, 8, 10... — kuṟiñci)
//   நித்திலக்கோவை    (a wider mix — marutam, neytal, mullai)
//
// Each poem has: number, poet, speaker (the dramatic voice), turai (situation),
// thinai (landscape), Tamil text (multi-line), transliteration, English
// translation, Tamil urai (commentary), alt English translation, historical/
// literary note.
// =============================================================================

