    note: "Composed by Kapilar, the great kuṟiñci poet of the Sangam age. Kapilar is so identified with kuṟiñci poems that his name appears repeatedly in this landscape. The poem is set in the convention of the secret love (kaḷavu) before marriage: the heroine and her lover meet in the mountain country, and the friend (tōḻi) is the only confidante. The 'kuṟiñci song' is itself a genre — sung in praise of the heroine's union — and the friend here describes singing it as part of celebrating the lover's coming."
