    altTranslation: "The kōṅku bloomed on the mountain;\nthe bee-humming grove — the rains;\n'Come' says — the rain;\n'Come' says — the wind;\n'Come' says — the kōṅku;\n'Come' says — your own heart;\n'Come' says — your beloved;\nsay 'Come' — to the marriage!",
