    altTranslation: "Again the summer road — I must go;\none house — one girl — I left behind;\nmullai fragrance in the heart — yāḻ-sound;\none promise — one hope — I gave;\nshe said 'come' through her love;\none memory — one direction — I walk;\nthe rains will come — one return;\none love — now and always — one!",
    note: "The pālai hero must leave again — 'mīṇṭum' (again) opens the poem, acknowledging that this is not a single separation but a recurring one. Wealth must be earned over and over; the wasteland must be crossed again and again. But the love that is 'now and always one' survives each departure and each return. The recurring journey does not diminish the love; it tests it."
