    transliteration: "Kuṉṟattil kōṅku kār kālam;\nVēṅkai vaṇṭu moykum cōlai;\nOru kātalaṉ — yāḻ kaṭal malai;\nOru tirumpal illāṉ — yāḻ kaṭal malai;\nMīṇṭum mīṇṭum — yāḻ kaṭal malai — varuvāṉ;\nOru maṇam oru vāḻvu — yāḻ kaṭal malai;\nĀṟṟu — neñcē — yāḻ kaṭal malai;\nOru nāṉ oru nī — eṉṟum — yāḻ kaṭal malai!",
    english: "The kōṅku on the mountain — the rains;\nthe vēṅkai grove swarms with bees;\none beloved — yāḻ, sea, mountain;\nhe who never turns away — yāḻ, sea, mountain;\nagain and again — yāḻ, sea, mountain — he will come;\none marriage, one life — yāḻ, sea, mountain;\nendure — O heart — yāḻ, sea, mountain;\none I, one you — always — yāḻ, sea, mountain!",
    tamilUrai: "கபிலர் குறிஞ்சி திணை. 'ஒரு நான் ஒரு நீ என்றும் யாழ் கடல் மலை' என்ற இறுதி. 'ஆற்று நெஞ்சே யாழ் கடல் மலை' — யாழ் கடல் மலை அளவு ஆற்று. இப்போது 'ஆற்று' என்ற கட்டளையும் மூன்று வரிசைகளால் வலுவூட்டப்படுகிறது. 'ஒரு நான் ஒரு நீ என்றும் யாழ் கடல் மலை' — என்றும் யாழ் கடல் மலை.",
    altTranslation: "The kōṅku on the mountain — the rains;\nthe vēṅkai grove swarms with bees;\none beloved — yāḻ, sea, mountain;\nhe who never turns away — yāḻ, sea, mountain;\nagain and again — yāḻ, sea, mountain — he will come;\none marriage, one life — yāḻ, sea, mountain;\nendure — O heart — yāḻ, sea, mountain;\none I, one you — always — yāḻ, sea, mountain!",
    note: "The friend's final formula: 'one I, one you, always, yāḻ-sea-mountain.' The three-metaphor phrase has become the predicate for the central declaration. What is the love that is always one? It is yāḻ-sea-mountain — musical, vast, and firm. The instruction to the heart — 'endure, O heart, yāḻ-sea-mountain' — asks for an endurance that is musical in its constancy, oceanic in its depth, and mountainous in its permanence."
