    altTranslation: "Rain-mountain kōṅku — the rains;\none woman, one eye, one world;\nalways with you — yāḻ, sea, mountain;\nagain and again with you — yāḻ, sea, mountain;\none night, one mountain — with you;\none love, one world — with you;\nagain and again, anew — with you;\none I, one you — always — with you!",
    note: "The word 'with you' (uṉṉōṭu) becomes the destination of all the sequences: 'always with you,' 'again and again with you,' 'anew with you,' 'always with you.' All the earlier declarations — one I one you, always one, again and again, anew, yāḻ-sea-mountain — were building toward this simple preposition: with. Love is being-with, and that being-with is always, renewed, musical, vast, firm."
