    transliteration: "Kuṉṟattil kōṅku malarntatu;\nVēṅkai vaṇṭu moykum cōlai;\nOru kātalaṉ vantāṉ — uṉṉōṭu;\nOru maṉam tantāṉ — yāḻ kaṭal malai;\nOru ulakam kaṭṭiṉāṉ — uṉṉōṭu;\nMīṇṭum varuvāṉ — uṉṉōṭu — putiṭāy;\nOru tirumpal illāṉ — yāḻ kaṭal malai;\nĀṟṟu — neñcē — uṉṉōṭu — eṉṟum!",
    english: "The kōṅku bloomed on the mountain;\nthe vēṅkai grove swarms with bees;\none beloved came — with you;\nhe gave one mind — yāḻ, sea, mountain;\nhe built one world — with you;\nhe will come again — with you — anew;\nhe who never turns away — yāḻ, sea, mountain;\nendure — O heart — with you — always!",
