    altTranslation: "The kōṅku bloomed on the mountain;\nthe vēṅkai grove swarms with bees;\none beloved came — with you;\nhe gave one mind — yāḻ, sea, mountain;\nhe built one world — with you;\nhe will come again — with you — anew;\nhe who never turns away — yāḻ, sea, mountain;\nendure — O heart — with you — always!",
    note: "The friend's instruction reaches its fullest form: 'endure, O heart, with you, always.' The heart is asked to endure not in isolation but in companionship — 'with you' applies not just to the beloved but to the heart itself. The heart endures with the beloved as its companion, held in the form of yāḻ-sea-mountain. Endurance is not lonely when the beloved is always present within."
