    altTranslation: "The rains came — mullai bloomed;\none way — I returned;\nthe heroine — one house — one doorway;\none face — yāḻ, sea, mountain — honey;\nyāḻ, sea, mountain — honey — she;\nyāḻ, sea, mountain — honey — I;\none life — yāḻ, sea, mountain — honey;\none love — yāḻ, sea, mountain — honey!",
    note: "The pālai return with the final identification: one love, yāḻ-sea-mountain, honey. Not like honey, not honey-like — but honey itself. The face seen at the doorway is yāḻ-sea-mountain-honey; both the beloved and the hero are yāḻ-sea-mountain-honey; the life and the love are yāḻ-sea-mountain-honey. The entire journey has been gathering this honey, and now it is held."
