    altTranslation: "The paddy-field — endless — ripened;\nthe lotus tank — endless — bloomed;\none heart — endless — waited;\none husband — endless — not there;\none house — endless — bitterness;\none woman — endless — joy — life — integrity;\ndream and hope — endless — always;\nyāḻ, sea, mountain — honey — endless — one!",
    note: "Veḷḷivīti's final word for the marutam wife: yāḻ-sea-mountain-honey, endless, one. She drops 'always' and ends with 'one' — matching Ammūvaṉār's kuṟiñci endings. The marutam wife's integrity is one with the kuṟiñci hero's love: both are endless, both are one. The anthology's five tiṇai meet at this point of identity — all are yāḻ-sea-mountain-honey, endless, one."
