    altTranslation: "The paddy-field — endless — ripened;\nthe lotus tank — endless — deep;\none heart — endless — waited;\none husband — endless — not there;\none house — endless — solitude;\none woman — endless — joy — life — memory — integrity;\ndream and hope — endless;\nyāḻ, sea, mountain — honey — endless — always — one!",
    note: "The marutam tradition closes with this: one woman, endless joy-life-memory-integrity; dream and hope, endless; yāḻ-sea-mountain-honey, endless, always, one. The paddy-field's endlessness, the tank's endless depth, the heart's endless waiting — all find their answer in the woman's endless inner life. The marutam tradition's final claim: the wronged wife is as complete and inexhaustible as the greatest love."
